[I] Mount a directory elsewhere with changed permissions

[T] bindfs is a FUSE filesystem for mirroring a directory to another
[T] directory, similarly to mount --bind, while altering the permissions in
[T] various ways. It can make a directory read-only, share it with a list of
[T] users or groups, or modify permission bits with chmod-like rules.

[U] https://bindfs.org/

[A] Martin Pärtel <martin.partel@gmail.com>
[M] Paul Manners <paul.manners@yahoo.com>

